{"acceptance_length": 9.159090909090908, "acceptance_lengths": [8, 3, 1, 4, 9, 3, 3, 2, 11, 8, 3, 15, 8, 8, 3, 14, 4, 5, 4, 8, 15, 15, 1, 16, 4, 16, 7, 16, 16, 8, 5, 4, 3, 5, 8, 16, 16, 16, 16, 14, 16, 16, 16, 14], "accepted_draft_lengths": [7, 2, 0, 3, 8, 2, 2, 1, 10, 7, 2, 14, 7, 7, 2, 13, 3, 4, 3, 7, 14, 14, 0, 15, 3, 15, 6, 15, 15, 7, 4, 3, 2, 4, 7, 15, 15, 15, 15, 13, 15, 15, 15, 13], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23321325568, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23321308160, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "We are given the following information:\n\n- Each **pepper** costs **$15**.\n- A **watermelon** costs **3 times** what a pepper costs.\n- An **orange** costs **$5 less** than a watermelon.\n- Dillon buys:\n  - 4 watermelons\n  - 20 peppers\n  - 10 oranges\n\nWe are to find the **total amount of money** Dillon will spend.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Find the cost of a watermelon\n\nSince a watermelon costs **3 times** what a pepper costs:\n\n$$\n\\text{Cost of watermelon} = 3 \\times \\text{Cost of pepper} = 3 \\times 15 = 45 \\text{ dollars}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find the cost of an orange\n\nAn orange costs **$5 less** than a watermelon:\n\n$$\n\\text{Cost of orange} = \\text{Cost of watermelon} - 5 = 45 - 5 = 40 \\text{ dollars}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the total cost for each item\n\n- **Watermelons**:  \n  $$\n  4 \\times 45 = 180 \\text{ dollars}\n  $$\n\n- **Peppers**:  \n  $$\n  20 \\times 15 = 300 \\text{ dollars}\n  $$\n\n- **Oranges**:  \n  $$\n  10 \\times 40 = 400 \\text{ dollars}\n  $$\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Add up all the costs\n\n$$\n\\text{Total cost} = 180 + 300 + 400 = \\boxed{880} \\text{ dollars}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{880}\n$$", "decode_seconds": 1.6130423191934824, "draft_calls": 44, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 112, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "ece1269540becf19b73b75b0ca48a5dfd6178ffe372c6606870efbbab8ae580a", "method": "relay_base", "output_hash": "50d542997f85a820cc30a116c3f8a112