{"acceptance_length": 6.735849056603773, "acceptance_lengths": [2, 7, 3, 3, 5, 8, 1, 5, 8, 8, 5, 2, 2, 3, 4, 15, 3, 4, 2, 7, 3, 16, 9, 15, 3, 1, 12, 3, 3, 16, 1, 4, 14, 16, 5, 1, 2, 15, 16, 16, 7, 3, 2, 3, 1, 3, 16, 10, 16, 8, 9, 1, 10], "accepted_draft_lengths": [1, 6, 2, 2, 4, 7, 0, 4, 7, 7, 4, 1, 1, 2, 3, 14, 2, 3, 1, 6, 2, 15, 8, 14, 2, 0, 11, 2, 2, 15, 0, 3, 13, 15, 4, 0, 1, 14, 15, 15, 6, 2, 1, 2, 0, 2, 15, 9, 15, 7, 8, 0, 9], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23321325568, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23321308160, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "We are given the following information:\n\n- Shiela bought **5 cell phones**, each costing **$150**.\n- She is paying in **3-month installments**.\n- A **2% interest** is charged for each unit.\n- We are to find out **how much Shiela will pay each month** for 3 months.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the total cost of the cell phones\n\nEach cell phone costs $150, and she bought 5 of them:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total cost} = 5 \\times 150 = 750 \\text{ dollars}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the total interest\n\nA 2% interest is charged for each unit. Since she bought 5 units, the total interest is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total interest} = 5 \\times (150 \\times 0.02) = 5 \\times 3 = 15 \\text{ dollars}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the total amount to be paid\n\n$$\n\\text{Total amount} = \\text{Total cost} + \\text{Total interest} = 750 + 15 = 765 \\text{ dollars}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Calculate the monthly payment\n\nShe is paying in **3 equal monthly installments**:\n\n$$\n\\text{Monthly payment} = \\frac{765}{3} = 255 \\text{ dollars}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{255}\n$$\n\nShiela will pay **$255** each month for 3 months.", "decode_seconds": 1.9414579747244718, "draft_calls": 53, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 72, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "ece1269540becf19b73b75b0ca48a5dfd6178ffe372c6606870efbbab8ae580a", "method": "relay_base", "output_hash": "4024e3f3d06918d37216a58