{"acceptance_length": 8.115384615384615, "acceptance_lengths": [4, 5, 6, 2, 1, 5, 2, 1, 9, 6, 16, 14, 5, 11, 2, 1, 4, 3, 1, 3, 2, 4, 12, 5, 16, 3, 1, 6, 16, 16, 9, 2, 3, 5, 2, 15, 16, 9, 16, 13, 16, 16, 16, 16, 16, 16, 7, 16, 14, 4, 7, 6], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23321325568, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23321308160, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "We are given that Gary bought a boat for **$9000**, and it **depreciates** by different percentages each year:\n\n- **Year 1:** 30% depreciation  \n- **Year 2:** 30% depreciation  \n- **Year 3:** 20% depreciation  \n\nWe are to find the **value of the boat after 3 years**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Depreciation in Year 1 (30%)\n\nDepreciation = 30% of $9000  \n$$\n\\text{Depreciation} = 0.30 \\times 9000 = 2700\n$$  \nNew value after Year 1:  \n$$\n9000 - 2700 = 6300\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Depreciation in Year 2 (30%)\n\nNow, the value is **$6300**.  \nDepreciation = 30% of $6300  \n$$\n\\text{Depreciation} = 0.30 \\times 6300 = 1890\n$$  \nNew value after Year 2:  \n$$\n6300 - 1890 = 4410\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Depreciation in Year 3 (20%)\n\nNow, the value is **$4410**.  \nDepreciation = 20% of $4410  \n$$\n\\text{Depreciation} = 0.20 \\times 4410 = 882\n$$  \nNew value after Year 3:  \n$$\n4410 - 882 = 3528\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{3528}\n$$\n\nSo, the boat is worth **$3528** after 3 years.", "decode_seconds": 1.8824500190094116, "draft_calls": 52, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 85, "method": "native_target_dflash", "output_hash": "d10122ac540e31260ae98737136c9e905b6d68c7a496f63d092cc8208f82c2ff", "output_tokens": 421, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23464267264, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23752343552, "problem_id": "gsm8k/0200e6459433efc5", "profile_regions_ms": {"unattributed_runtime": 1922.0569301396608}, "rank": 0, "reference_answer": "3528", "repetition": 0, "request_seconds": 1.9220569301396608, "reserved_memory_after_bytes": 23752343552, "reserved_memo