{"acceptance_length": 7.225806451612903, "acceptance_lengths": [3, 3, 2, 2, 1, 5, 4, 6, 2, 4, 3, 10, 1, 3, 5, 4, 2, 6, 5, 7, 5, 16, 4, 16, 16, 16, 16, 10, 3, 2, 3, 11, 2, 3, 4, 5, 1, 8, 1, 10, 2, 16, 11, 5, 12, 14, 16, 16, 5, 16, 16, 16, 3, 3, 10, 4, 16, 2, 1, 16, 9, 9], "accepted_draft_lengths": [2, 2, 1, 1, 0, 4, 3, 5, 1, 3, 2, 9, 0, 2, 4, 3, 1, 5, 4, 6, 4, 15, 3, 15, 15, 15, 15, 9, 2, 1, 2, 10, 1, 2, 3, 4, 0, 7, 0, 9, 1, 15, 10, 4, 11, 13, 15, 15, 4, 15, 15, 15, 2, 2, 9, 3, 15, 1, 0, 15, 8, 8], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23321325568, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23321308160, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "We are given the number of each baked good and their individual lengths, and we are to find the **total length** of all baked goods **end to end**, in **feet**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Convert all lengths to the same unit (feet)\n\n- **Each roll is 4 inches long**  \n  Since 1 foot = 12 inches,  \n  $$\n  4 \\text{ inches} = \\frac{4}{12} = \\frac{1}{3} \\text{ feet}\n  $$\n\n- **Each croissant is 6 inches long**  \n  $$\n  6 \\text{ inches} = \\frac{6}{12} = \\frac{1}{2} \\text{ feet}\n  $$\n\n- **Each baguette is 2 feet long**  \n  Already in feet, so no conversion needed.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the total length for each type of baked good\n\n- **Rolls:**  \n  Bill bakes 300 rolls, each $ \\frac{1}{3} $ feet long  \n  $$\n  300 \\times \\frac{1}{3} = 100 \\text{ feet}\n  $$\n\n- **Croissants:**  \n  Bill bakes 120 croissants, each $ \\frac{1}{2} $ feet long  \n  $$\n  120 \\times \\frac{1}{2} = 60 \\text{ feet}\n  $$\n\n- **Baguettes:**  \n  Bill bakes 60 baguettes, each 2 feet long  \n  $$\n  60 \\times 2 = 120 \\text{ feet}\n  $$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Add up all the lengths\n\n$$\n100 \\text{ feet} + 60 \\text{ feet} + 120 \\text{ feet} = 280 \\text{ feet}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{280} \\text{ feet}\n$$", "decode_seconds": 2.2751355920918286, "draft_calls": 62, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 101, 