{"acceptance_length": 8.241379310344827, "acceptance_lengths": [14, 12, 5, 6, 2, 9, 6, 6, 1, 6, 8, 4, 5, 8, 4, 10, 14, 6, 11, 10, 16, 2, 14, 4, 7, 10, 16, 16, 7], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23321325568, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23321308160, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "We are given:\n\n- A class of **200 students** is split into **3 groups**.\n- **2 of the groups are equal in number**.\n- The **third group (smallest)** is **10 less than each of the other two groups**.\n\nLet\u2019s define the number of students in the **two equal groups** as $ x $.\n\nThen, the **smallest group** has $ x - 10 $ students.\n\nNow, the total number of students is:\n\n$$\nx + x + (x - 10) = 200\n$$\n\nSimplify:\n\n$$\n3x - 10 = 200\n$$\n\nAdd 10 to both sides:\n\n$$\n3x = 210\n$$\n\nDivide by 3:\n\n$$\nx = 70\n$$\n\nSo, the two equal groups have **70 students each**, and the smallest group has:\n\n$$\nx - 10 = 70 - 10 = \\boxed{60}\n$$\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{60}\n$$", "decode_seconds": 1.0458207339979708, "draft_calls": 29, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 85, "method": "native_target_dflash", "output_hash": "1ac2b3eecf0cafc2f99df33b0ab5393e06950b3f99fa1ea2c07f791351dbc780", "output_tokens": 238, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23402915840, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23752343552, "problem_id": "gsm8k/068ad465dc69dcf1", "profile_regions_ms": {"unattributed_runtime": 1085.3491290472448}, "rank": 0, "reference_answer": "60", "repetition": 0, "request_seconds": 1.0853491290472448, "reserved_memory_after_bytes": 23752343552, "reserved_memory_before_bytes": 23752343552, "target_calls": 29, "time_to_first_token_seconds": 0.03273179428651929, "turn_index": 0}
