{"acceptance_length": 6.310344827586207, "acceptance_lengths": [3, 11, 6, 2, 5, 2, 2, 1, 2, 6, 6, 5, 4, 5, 9, 15, 4, 6, 6, 6, 2, 4, 11, 8, 12, 10, 6, 5, 6, 2, 7, 13, 16, 14, 2, 3, 7, 1, 4, 13, 12, 6, 9, 8, 2, 2, 6, 2, 1, 11, 11, 13, 11, 1, 3, 4, 5, 7], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23321325568, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23321308160, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "Let's break this down step by step to find the **cost per serving**.\n\n---\n\n### **1. Determine the amount of onions used:**\n\n- Antoine's recipe calls for **2 pounds** of onions.\n- He **doubles** that amount:  \n  $$\n  2 \\text{ pounds} \\times 2 = 4 \\text{ pounds}\n  $$\n\n---\n\n### **2. Calculate the cost of the onions:**\n\n- Onions are on sale for **$2.00 per pound**.  \n  $$\n  4 \\text{ pounds} \\times \\$2.00/\\text{pound} = \\$8.00\n  $$\n\n---\n\n### **3. Calculate the cost of the beef stock:**\n\n- He needs **2 boxes** of beef stock.\n- Each box costs **$2.00**.  \n  $$\n  2 \\text{ boxes} \\times \\$2.00/\\text{box} = \\$4.00\n  $$\n\n---\n\n### **4. Total cost of the ingredients:**\n\n$$\n\\$8.00 \\text{ (onions)} + \\$4.00 \\text{ (beef stock)} = \\$12.00\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **5. Determine the cost per serving:**\n\n- The soup serves **6 people**.\n- Total cost is **\\$12.00**.\n- Cost per serving:  \n  $$\n  \\frac{\\$12.00}{6} = \\$2.00\n  $$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{2}\n$$\n\nSo, the **cost per serving** is **\\$2.00**.", "decode_seconds": 2.1083503160625696, "draft_calls": 58, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 110, "method": "native_target_dflash", "output_hash": "4ccff9df5b280e8ee803d08dc7e2cee5d1f129814496f8d2f38bf70861657032", "output_tokens": 365, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23431382528, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23752343552, "problem_id": "gsm8k/0246c431c39aa335", "profile_regions_ms": {"unattributed_runtime": 2147.9329131543636}, "rank": 0, "reference_answer": "2", "repetition": 0, "request_seconds": 2.1479329131543636, "res